 The update method becomes very useful when working with arrays or objects when we want to modify a part of the array or the object without setting the wholevalue. For instance, we can write a function that adds a new name to the names signal:
const names = signal<string[]>([]);
const addName = (name: string) => names.update(value => [...value, name]);
addName('John');
console.log(names())
